description:
Filed from a downstream v1 -> re-frame2 migration's skills retrospective (a suggestion, not a work order). Verified at re-frame2 origin/main fd1d1565f1. Observed on a ~170-file Reagent app whose backend stack was down for this phase.

## Skill file and section

skills/re-frame-migration/references/runtime-smoke-test.md, loop step 0 (line 24) and the §Required to finish is not required to run worked case (line 66).

## What it says

- :24, step 0: list "the boot scenarios it supports (feature flags, auth modes, role or tenant variants, a deep-link boot)".
- :66, worked case: "The live boot needs an authenticated session nobody has supplied ... Report the boot smoke **pending: needs an authenticated session**".

## What happened (generic)

The leaf treats a missing backend or session as all or nothing: the whole boot smoke is reported pending. But an app with no backend still boots. It runs its boot machine to its failure state and renders its own failure screen, and much of the checklist can be verified on that path. The worker booted the dev build against a static dev server only. The auth request 404'd, and the app went `fetch-jwt -> failed-jwt -> failed-bootstrap` to its "couldn't start" screen. It produced the same 12-epoch sequence on every boot and on two browser versions. From that path it verified:

- the boot machine's terminal state (`read-sub [:rf/machine <boot-id>]` -> `:state :failed`, with the `:rf.machine/started` trace);
- the frame's interceptor chain, in order, against the plan;
- the seed event and the mount (`createRoot`, frame provider);
- the first-screen subs of the failure screen;
- a clean console and trace (no `:rf.error/*` or `:rf.warning/*`);
- the async entry points the failure screen still installs: `window 'error'`, keydown, popstate, a keyboard-shim timer and the XHR failure callbacks.

Out of 117 checklist rows, 16 were verified and 11 split (the reachable half verified). The remaining 69 stayed pending on the stack, and none failed.

## Evidence

- The worker's B0 record: an epoch chain identical on every boot, `:app/boot` at `{:state :failed ...}`, and no framework diagnostics in the console, CDP exceptions, the unfiltered trace buffer or any retained epoch's trace events.
- De-dup: rf2-jtxpo (closed) added step 0's page and scenario enumeration, but no item covers a no-backend boot. Searches for "no backend", "failure path"/"failure screen" with "smoke", and "standalone boot" found nothing relevant.

## Suggested change

Add a "standalone boot (no backend)" scenario to step 0, and a sentence to the worked case. When the backend or session is missing, still boot to the app's own failure path and verify:

- each boot machine's terminal state;
- the frame chain;
- the seed slots and the subs the failure screen reads;
- the console and the trace;
- the async entry points the failure screen still installs.

Report those rows as verified, and only the rest as pending on the named prerequisite. The point is that "pending" applies per row, not to the whole smoke.
